␀$␀2␀DFLT␀latn␀␀␀␀␀␀ÿÿ␀␀␀␀tnum␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀F␀ ␀ƒ␀„␀…␀†␀‡␀ˆ␀‰␀Š␀‹␀Œ␀‘␀’␀•␀–␀“␀”␀—␀␀Ž␀␀␀˜␀™␀š␀›␀œ␀␀ž␀Ÿ␀ ␀¡␀¢␀␀␀y␀‚␀␀␀¨␀­␀
␀µ␀µ␀␀Á␀Â␀␀Ä␀Å␀␀Ë␀Ò␀␀Ö␀Ö␀␀ó␀ô␀# Defensive formations.
#   pos: depth-chart group (DE, DT, LB, CB, S)
#   at:  [x, y] relative to the ball: x = yards off the ball, y = yards right (+) / left (-)
#   over: align on an offensive receiver instead of a fixed spot:
#         "#1 left" = widest receiver on the left, "#2 right" = second from the outside on the right,
#         "#2 strong" / "#2 weak" = side with more / fewer receivers, "back" / "back2" = backfield players
#   depth / inside: yards off the ball and yards inside of that receiver
# Plays can override any alignment.

base_43:
  title: 4-3 Base
  description: 4-3 base (4 DL, 3 LB, 2 CB, 2 S)
